original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["EN4-URA-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Independently annotate a short story for two theme strands and one symbol: quote/paraphrase evidence, write a paragraph analysis, and note one alternative reading you considered and rejected. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Sample: original example using theme on new material; names a specific word, source or choice and explains its effect.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Sample error: Declaring a theme with no pattern of evidence, or insisting a symbol means the same thing in every text.. Correction: Strong answer: claim is text-specific;. Why it helps the audience is stated.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Declaring a theme with no pattern of evidence, or insisting a symbol means the same thing in every text. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Produce a fresh example demonstrating theme on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Name one likely error with theme, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Accept original work about theme with a specific supporting detail. Reject copied model wording with no new material. / Accept a misconception, a correction, and a purpose-linked reason for theme. Reject corrections that do not change the inaccurate idea..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"This matches the taught method for theme. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Ignore the words and invent a more exciting event.","Skip the prompt because the first idea sounded good.","claim is text-